 "relevance_note": "Single case report of a girl with genetically confirmed Danon disease: \"identified a novel heterozygous frameshift variant(ex.7_9del site) in the LAMP-2 gene\".",
 "method_note": "Built by hand with a short script; no tables in the paper. One in-scope person, labelled 'patient' (rule 5). Contradiction in the paper: the case text says 'A 12-year-old female patient' and 'Her maternal history', but the consent statement says 'as he is an under-aged child'; sex recorded as female from the case text, flagged here. 'Her maternal history is notable for cardiomegaly' does not identify a specific relative (mother vs maternal family unclear) and gives no testing, so no relative row was created. Variant printed only as 'ex.7_9del site' (no transcript, cDNA or protein); variant type 'frameshift' and zygosity 'heterozygous' are as the authors state; they call it 'novel' and not in HGMD but give no pathogenicity class, so pathogenicity is not reported. No parental testing reported. Age 12 recorded as age at last evaluation (age at presentation); no age at diagnosis stated. CMR EF 70% and LVEDD 45 mm were not interpreted; the composite checklist item 'dilated or hypokinetic left ventricle' stays not reported because only dilation is explicitly excluded ('without left ventricular hypertrophy or dilation'). No treatment reported.",
